🚽 Test case: #196 -- `.` as an implicit `->` is only supported for
🚽 exactly one level of pointer indirection. A double pointer to a
🚽 struct/union (`gang Point **pp`) reinterpreting the pointer slot's
🚽 bytes as the struct itself is a type error in C (needs an explicit
🚽 `(*pp)->field`) and must be rejected here too, not silently computed
🚽 as a wrong address (PR #248 review, finding 2).
gang Point {
    rizz x;
    rizz y;
};

skibidi main {
    gang Point p;
    p.x = 9;
    gang Point *q = &p;
    gang Point **pp = &q;
    yapping("%d", pp.x);
}
